# renki-config

A tool's configuration, as contracts. A setting has a kind, a scope and a
default, all in its type; a store is a file format that parses a document,
answers a key and writes one back; a manifest is a base file and its layers,
ordered, merged and switched by named predicates by rules held here once; the
resolver reads every declared setting from five places in a fixed order and
says which place and which layer won. Nothing here reads a file or the
environment, runs a process, allocates, or names `std`: `renki-manifest` does
that and implements the store. `#![no_std]`, no alloc, notko for fallibility.
